From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] Use Python 3 for the original Python 3 table generator
Upstream-source: https://github.com/jaseg/lolcat/blob/a9ab81839f2a00fa1d831648a1d79e268bb1ddac/Makefile
License: WTFPL
Reason: The original generator uses Python 3 f-strings while the root Makefile
invokes an unversioned python command. Explicit python3 preserves the original
generator and default all/install features on the target distribution.
Upstream-status: not-submitted
Remove-when: The stable upstream root Makefile explicitly invokes python3.
Validation: Data-only GNU zero-fuzz byte delta; exact original Makefile digest
is required in %prep. Target regeneration must reproduce the original header.
No algorithm, table, tests, flags, notices or feature removal.

--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -16 +16 @@
-	python $< > $@
+	python3 $< > $@
